Added opt-in managed block commit fees, enabled by setting `burnchain.block_commit_replacement_fee_max_sats` (requires `burnchain.rbf_fee_increment = 0`): the miner raises the fee of a pending block commit when the target rises, prices replacements at the minimum Bitcoin requires (capped at this amount), resends the same transaction after an ambiguous broadcast failure, and optionally prices commits by actual size via `burnchain.block_commit_fee_rate_sat_per_kvb`. Miners that don't set it are unaffected.
